# GammaBayes 2.1.1

## Fixes
- `GammaLogExposure`: `pointing_dirs=None` and `live_times=None` no longer crash; live times given in any
  unit are converted once (the unit converter double-counted non-second units); `__call__` no longer
  adds the unit converter a second time, and returns `log(smallest normal number)` instead of `-inf`
  for zero exposure so model cubes stay finite and `logaddexp` gradients stay NaN-free
  (`log_exposure_map` itself still holds `-inf`); `+` works (a `Quantity` reached `torch.log`, and the
  unit ratio was inverted); construction from an existing `log_exposure_map` works.
- `GammaBinning`: `__eq__` on the edges (exposures / priors on identical geometries combine),
  `__repr__`, `padded(pads)` (true-space geometry for `IRFForwardConv`).
- `IRFExtractor`: explicit `irf_time_seconds=` (0.5 h / 5 h / 50 h prod5 optimisation; the default keeps
  the 5 h file -- `observation_time` never selected the file), `pointing_dir` stored, `irf_file_path`
  attribute, clear `NotImplementedError` for `instrument='HESS'`, `log_aeff` / `log_bkg_CCR` /
  `log_edisp` / `log_psf` return tensors in the input dtype and device, `plot_edisp_*` had true and
  reconstructed energies swapped.
- `extract_galprop_components`: energy axis off by one plane (`CRVAL3 + CDELT3*NAXIS3` endpoint);
  `component='all'` returns the summed template instead of a tuple; FoV margin used `lon_res` (bins per
  degree) as a width.
- `IsotropicPowerLaw` / `IsotropicBrokenPowerLaw` rewritten on the 2.x component API (were unusable).
- `StaticSourceDistTemplate`: wrong attribute name when built from a log template.
- `utils.integration.construct_log_dx`: 0-d `torch.cat`, log-uniform bin width, torch `logsumexp`.
- `CTAO_irf_file_utils`: no bare `except` around the IRF tar extraction.
- `SingleChannelDMPrior`: default `channel='W+W-'` (the old default `'W'` was a PPPC column name that only
  worked through the PPPC fallback).
- Docstrings reviewed throughout the torch core; the IRF wrappers now state which quantities are true and
  which reconstructed (the cosmic-ray background is tabulated in reconstructed energy and position).

## Apple silicon (MPS)
- Device / dtype hygiene for backends without float64: forward-operator kernels are built on the CPU
  in float64 and cast to the default dtype / device (`make_forward_irf_kernels(..., device=)`);
  `GammaBinning.padded`, exposures, the DM spectral tables and GALPROP templates follow
  `torch.get_default_dtype()`.

## Performance
- `RegularTorchInterpolator` caches the table per device (it was copied on every call).
- DM spectral tables (CosmiXs / PPPC / QCDUNC) are parsed once per process instead of once per channel.
- `IRFKernelDist.sample_kernel` vectorised (was a Python loop over every voxel).

## Packaging
- `python_requires >= 3.10`; `regions >= 0.9, < 0.11` (gammapy <= 2.1); `[docs]` / `[test]` extras;
  `QCDUNC_Tables` shipped; `MANIFEST.IN` matches the tree; CI on Python 3.10-3.13 installs the package
  with its own requirements.

## Documentation
- Rewritten for 2.x: getting-started pages (installation, concepts, migration from 0.x), six executable
  tutorials (geometry, IRFs and exposure, source components and batching, dark matter, forward IRF
  operator, an end-to-end profile-likelihood search), autodoc API reference split into the torch core
  and the legacy layer, `docs/run_notebooks.sh` + `docs/annotate_timings.py` (execute the tutorials and
  stamp per-cell wall times).  The tutorials run on CPU, CUDA or Apple MPS (`GAMMABAYES_DOCS_DEVICE`);
  tutorial 06 profiles the nuisance amplitudes with an analytic Newton template fit, with and without a
  per-energy-bin background systematic, in seconds on a laptop CPU.  The 0.x notebooks moved to
  `docs/legacy_tutorials/`.

## Tests
- `src/gammabayes/tests/test_review_fixes.py` (10 tests, no data files); the 0.x top-level `tests/`
  directory (numpy-era, pinned to astropy 5 / gammapy 1.1) is removed and CI runs the package tests.


# GammaBayes 2.1.0 (torch port)

## Breaking changes
- `SingleDMSpectralComp` now **requires** `mass=` at call time (the old `partial(..., mass=1)` default is gone).
- Component outputs carry a leading batch axis `(B, ...)`. `DiscreteLogPrior.eval_log_on_geom(squeeze=True)`
  (the default) drops `B == 1`, so existing single-point callers are unaffected.
- Dependencies moved to numpy 2 / astropy 6 / gammapy 2.
- Downstream projects that pin an API version should bump it.

## Batched evaluation
- New `core/batching.py`: `as_param`, `batch_size`, `promote_batch`, `iter_batch_chunks`.
- TLDR of how data/parameter variables scale now: parameters are scalar or `(B,)`; spectral components return `(B, E)`, spatial `(B, lon, lat)`, rate cubes `(B, E, lon, lat)`.
- (BIG CHANGE) `RegularTorchInterpolator` vectorisation: query tensors of any shape, broadcast against each other (e.g. `(B, 1)` mass x `(1, E)` energy -> `(B, E)`); device-aware; edge clamping unchanged.
- Batched (in line with above): `PowerLaw`, `ExpCutoffPowerLaw`, `BrokenPowerLaw`, `BroadBrokenPowerLaw`, `LogParabola`, `PointSpatial_PriorComp`, `GaussianSpatial_PriorComp`, `IsotropicSpatial_PriorComp`, `SingleDMSpectralComp` (mass / kappa / delta); `DM_Profile`; `CustomDMRatiosModel`; `SingleChannelDMPrior`,`TwoCompFluxPrior`.
- `DM_Profile.logdiffJ`: profile kwargs scalar or `(B,)` -> `(B, S)`; chunked LOS integral (`max_elems`) with gradient checkpointing, so chunking also bounds memory under autograd (about 2x LOS cost in backward), rho(r_sun) re-anchored to the local density for the current shape parameters.
- `CustomDMRatiosModel`: ratios as a dict or `(B, n_ch)` tensor; `log_spectrum`, `log_J`; spectral and J caches that are bypassed whenever an input carries autograd state, and only used for small batches.
- `SourceFluxDiscreteLogPrior` caches the exposure cube per geometry (`_log_exposure_on`).

## IRF convolution memory (legacy operator)
- `LogSumExpConv3D.forward` is separable (spatial `conv2d` + log-space energy pass): peak memory `O(B E S K_d)` instead of `O(B E S K^3)`; `max_batch=` chunks over B. The old path is kept as `forward_reference`. Both `binning_geometry` and the historical `binnning_geometry` kwarg are accepted; `padding=None` -> `k // 2`.
- Per-energy spatial kernels: `LogSumExpConv3D(energy_kernel=(K_d,), spatial_kernel=(E, K_h, K_w))`.
- Semantics are unchanged (per-output normalisation, not count conserving). Edge-bin values can differ at the rounding level from the reference path; updating is recommended for bit-level consistency in regression checks.

## Energy-dependent PSF
- `IRFExtractor.psf_containment_radius(E, offset, fraction)`: containment radius from the tabulated PSF.
- `IRFExtractor.psf_sigma_vs_energy(geom, fraction, weighting='aeff'|'uniform'|'counts', counts, pixel_floor)`:
  FoV-averaged Gaussian-equivalent sigma(E_true).
- `make_spatial_kernel_per_energy(geom, sigma_deg, clearance)`, `make_irf_kernel_per_energy(...)`.

## Fixes
- `extract_galprop_components(component='all')` called a non-existent function with an undefined name.
- `DiscreteLogPrior._cached_rates` was never initialised.
- `GammaLogExposure`: `raise NotImplemented` -> `NotImplementedError`; list `.append/.extend` on tensors ->
  `torch.cat`; `lives_times` kwarg typo; `torch.array_equiv` -> `torch.equal` on sorted pointings;
  stray `print`.
- `IRFKernelDist.sample_kernel`: lon/lat bounds used the energy-axis length.
- `BroadBrokenPowerLaw` (undefined `index`, `.value`); `LogParabola` (numpy calls, bad `self`).
- `CustomDMRatiosModel.__iter__ / items / keys` referenced a never-set attribute.
- `SingleDMSpectralComp`: a missing CosmiXs (kappa) or QCDUNC (delta) table now prints a one-time warning that the parameter has no effect, instead of silently doing nothing. The QCDUNC table is found under either `AtProduction-Ga.dat` or `AtProduction-Ga-Combined-Up-QCDUNC.dat`.
- New `assert_slots_exist(models_by_name, slots)` in `core/utils.py`: fails loudly on a slot -> source map that points at a missing source.

## Count-conserving IRF forward operator
- New `utils/irf_forward.py`:
  - `bin_prob_kernel`: closed-form bin-to-bin migration probabilities, box (x) Gaussian (x) box via
    `G(x) = x Phi(x) + phi(x)`; rows sum to 1.
  - `make_forward_irf_kernels`: energy kernel (dex) plus a scalar or per-true-energy spatial kernel.
  - `IRFForwardConv`: maps a **padded true grid** to the reco grid ("valid" convolution). Expected counts are
    conserved apart from physical migration out of the analysis window. Spatial pass as a grouped `conv2d`
    per true-energy plane, energy pass linear with a per-pixel shift (no `-inf` gradients); log-space unfold
    fallback kept for testing; `dense_reference` for validation.
- `GammaBinning.from_edges(energy_edges, lon_edges, lat_edges, lon_res=None, lat_res=None)`: builds a geometry
  from exact edges (no `int(range*res + 1)` truncation), e.g. a padded copy of another geometry.
- `GammaLogExposure.refresh`: NaN log exposure (A_eff evaluated off its tabulated axis, e.g. on padded true
  energies) -> `-inf` instead of poisoning every rate cube.
- Exported from `gammabayes.utils` and `gammabayes.response_functions.core`.

## Packaging
- Version 2.1.0 (`__init__.py`, `setup.py`).
- `install_requires`: `numpy>=2.0`, `astropy>=6.1`, `gammapy>=2.0`, `h5py>=3.11`, `healpy>=1.17`,
  `torch>=2.4`, `scipy`; exact pins dropped for pytest, icecream, seaborn, requests and matplotlib.
- `package_data` now ships `dark_matter/CosmiXs_Tables/*.dat`.

## Tests
`pytest gammabayes/tests/ -q`. No data files needed.
- `test_batching.py`: batched vs looped evaluation for every component above.
- `test_logconv.py`: separable vs reference `LogSumExpConv3D`, per-energy kernels, chunking.
- `test_psf_energy.py`: containment radius / sigma(E), per-energy kernels.
- `test_irf_forward.py`: dense reference, per-energy PSF, count conservation, batching / gradients, log fallback, `from_edges`, empty-window gradients.

## Known issues (legacy modules)
- `HESSCatalogueSources_Prior.log_func` signature does not match `log_flux_function(grid, ...)`.
- `IsotropicPowerLaw` / `IsotropicBrokenPowerLaw` pass `spectral_class=` kwargs that `TwoCompFluxPrior` never accepted (fixed in 2.1.1).
- `hyper_inference/`, `samplers/`, `utils/cli/` are numpy-era and unmaintained.
